{"id":"e577b2f2-bb6b-457a-8d07-88807e9b2167","body":"PR up: https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/629 — one store parse per recall. `LoadWithIntegrity` serves records + integrity from a single `loadCombined`; the blind-spot explainer reuses that report (its seam takes an optional precomputed report; query/retrieve pass nil, unchanged).

Receipt decision (bullet 2): **keep the vitality serve receipt.** It is Phase 1 of the lifecycle ledger (`docs/vitality_receipts.md`); receipts are the evidence for the Phase 2 outcome join and Phase 3 decay — the "make it feed ranking" option, which is the COR-2311 follow-up direction. The write is best-effort/never-fails by contract, so the cost today is one cheap `git rev-parse` plus a lock-scoped append. Dropping it would orphan `memories vitality` and the documented plan.

Out of scope, confirmed: no BM25 postings sidecar; query/retrieve's own parse counts (brief's is COR-2314).","attachments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-10T19:32:42.175Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-10T19:32:42.068Z","parentId":null,"resolvedAt":null,"quotedText":null,"author":{"id":"bd1c458e-3bb3-4d0c-8ad7-e36f19afc156","name":"Evis Drenova"},"onBehalfOf":null}

